  "answer_text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (formerly known as Wake Forest Baptist Health). \n\nBased in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, it is a prominent academic medical center and health system that serves as the academic core of Atrium Health (which is part of the larger Advocate Health network).\n\nThe website serves as a primary hub for patients, medical students, researchers, and healthcare professionals. \n\n---\n\n### What You Can Do on WakeHealth.edu\n\n#### 1. Patient Services & Care\n* **Find a Doctor:** Search for primary care physicians, specialists, and other healthcare providers by name, specialty, or location.\n* **Access MyAtriumHealth (Patient Portal):** Log in to the patient portal (powered by Epic MyChart) to view medical records, request prescription refills, message your doctor, view test results, and pay medical bills online.\n* **Schedule Appointments:** Request or book appointments online for various clinical services.\n* **Find Locations:** Get directions, contact details, and hours of operation for the main medical center, emergency rooms, urgent care clinics, and specialty offices.\n\n#### 2. Academic & Research Resources\n* **Wake Forest School of Medicine:** Access information on medical degrees, physician assistant (PA) programs, academic departments, residency and fellowship training, and continuing medical education (CME).\n* **Research & Clinical Trials:** Learn about ongoing medical research, search for open clinical trials, and find information on the Innovation Quarter in Winston-Salem.\n\n#### 3. Key Facilities Highlighted on the Site\n* **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center:** The main 885-bed tertiary care teaching hospital.\n* **Brenner Children's Hospital:** The system\u2019s dedicated pediatric hospital.\n* **Community Hospitals:** Regional locations such as Davie, Lexington, Wilkes, and High Point medical centers.\n* **Level I Trauma Centers:** Information regarding the region's Level I Adult and Pediatric Trauma Center services.\n\n### Looking for something specific?\n* **For Patient Care & Appointments:** Navigate to the \"Get Care\" or \"MyAtriumHealth\" sections on the homepage.\n* **For Billing & Insurance:** Find accepted insurance plans and payment options under the financial resources tabs.\n* **For Careers:** Search job openings across the medical network.",
